data.content:
**Yes, C# fully supports `stackalloc`'d `Span<nint>` and `Span<nuint>`.** Both work as expected:

```csharp
Span<nint> values = stackalloc nint[5];
Span<nuint> unsigned = stackalloc nuint[3];
```

On this 64-bit system, `nint.Size` is 8 bytes (would be 4 on 32-bit). The native-sized integers (`nint`/`nuint`) are valid unmanaged types, so they satisfy the constraint for `stackalloc`. This has been supported since C# 9 / .NET 5 when `nint`/`nuint` were introduced.
